# ============================================================
# IMPORTANT PRIOR FINDINGS THAT MUST NOT BE LOST
# ============================================================

Use these as known QA lessons, not assumptions requiring rediscovery unless a check fails.

### HCC universe
- broad HCC ≈ 3,999
- high-confidence HCC ≈ 2,544

### Systemic therapy
v10 showed that "first observed systemic treatment in REACH" is NOT equivalent to true first-line.

Only approximately 282/569 previously labelled 1L episodes were high-confidence true first-line.

Never call something true 1L unless it passes the v10 true-first-line criteria.

### AFP
The v9 AFP result was wrong.

Correct strict tumor-marker components include principally:
- AFETOPROTEIN
- AFPTM
- AFPMKR

Correct v10 coverage:
- systemic-treated ever AFP ≈87.9%
- decision point −14d ≈72%
- −30d ≈79%
- −90d ≈85%
- any prior ≈88%

Do not revert to AFPTM-only logic.

Do NOT use note-extracted AFP as the primary measurement.

### Date shifting
Every patient's dates are shifted by one fixed offset of ≤6 months.

Therefore:

VALID:
- all within-patient ordering
- all within-patient intervals
- treatment duration
- time to next therapy
- baseline-to-follow-up intervals
- time to death
- time to decompensation

ABSOLUTE cross-patient calendar dates:
- bounded uncertainty ±6 months.

Use v10 robust-date logic where calendar era matters.

### Radiology
The v9 radiology parser was overly permissive.

Do not call a radiology phenotype validated merely because Genie rereads its own output.

Human validation is still required for research-grade radiology extraction.

### Manual validation terminology
IMPORTANT:

Genie is an AI system.

It may:
- produce an audit packet,
- perform an internal model spot-check,
- show evidence text.

It MUST NOT call its own review a:
- "human audit,"
- "manual gold standard,"
- "human validation."

Only the human investigator can perform those.

Use terminology:

`MODEL-ASSISTED AUDIT — REQUIRES HUMAN CONFIRMATION`

where appropriate.

